# Credential shape for bases-mcp.
//
// The runtime shape for every variable the binary reads lives at the repository
// root in `.env.schema`; this file is the DEPLOYMENT's credential shape — the
// WebDAV variables the renderer requests as podman secrets. It does not
// duplicate the transport or audit variables, which are set in `compose.yaml`.
// Names, types and examples; never a value.
//
// Production connects to OxiCloud over WebDAV (not rustfs, not a mounted
// vault). The filesystem backend (BASES_MCP_VAULT) is intentionally absent
// from this deployment schema: there is no vault volume mounted in the
// container, and a planted BASES_MCP_VAULT would make the binary choose the
// filesystem backend over WebDAV. `BASES_MCP_VAULT` remains available in the
// root `.env.schema` for local/stdio runs.

// @defaultSensitive=true
// @defaultRequired=true

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_URL
//   @sensitive
//   @required true
//   @type env
//   @example https://cloud.kroeppl.online/webdav/

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_USER
//   @sensitive
//   @required true
//   @type env
//   @auditIgnore

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD
//   @sensitive
//   @required true
//   @type env
//   @auditIgnore
